=== SURVEY ===
Target: VehicleUpgradesWidget (new widget) + registry entry
Hooks required:
  - useVehicleUpgrades(vehicleId) from @/api/hooks/useVehicles → returns VehicleInfoEnvelope<Record<string, unknown>>
  - useShareLinks(driveId) from @/api/hooks/useSharing → returns ShareToken[]
  - useDrives(vehicleId) from @/api/hooks/useDriving → needed to get recent driveId for share links
  - useVehicles() from @/api/hooks/useVehicles → fallback vehicleId
Existing widget patterns reviewed: SubscriptionsWidget, WidgetDetailCard, WidgetShell

=== REASONING ===
- Compact (1×2): Shows eligible upgrade count or "Up to date" green badge. Touch-friendly min-h-[44px].
- Standard (2×4): Two sections: upgrades list (name + price badge + description) with "All upgrades applied ✅" empty state,
  divider, then share links section showing active count + nearest expiry.
- Wide (3×4+): Adds per-upgrade eligibility detail text below description.
- useShareLinks requires a driveId → use useDrives(stringId) to get the most recent drive, extract its ID.
- All data null-safe: upgrades ?? [], shareLinks ?? []. All strings i18n via useTranslation('dashboard').
- All freshness props forwarded to WidgetShell.

